{
  "_doc": [
    "Concept taxonomy for semiconductor trend analysis.",
    "Each concept has a list of synonyms. Matching rules (see semitrend/matcher.py):",
    "  - Plain phrase (contains lowercase letters): case-insensitive; spaces/hyphens are interchangeable",
    "    and optional (so 'nano sheet' also matches 'nanosheet' and 'nano-sheet'); trailing plural allowed.",
    "  - Acronym (no lowercase letters, e.g. 'GAA', 'HBM3', '3D IC'): case-SENSITIVE whole-word match,",
    "    to avoid false positives from common words.",
    "  - 're:' prefix: raw regex, case-sensitive unless you use (?i).",
    "  - 'exclude' (optional): regex; a document matching it is NOT counted even if a synonym hits.",
    "  - 'require' (optional): regex; the document must ALSO match it (context gate, e.g. GaN only in power/RF context).",
    "  - 's2_extra' (optional): plain terms added to the Semantic Scholar search query only (regex synonyms",
    "    cannot be sent to the search engine, so list their plain forms here).",
    "Edit freely; the analysis re-runs from the cached raw data without re-fetching.",
    "'domain_terms' defines the corpus: it is sent as the OR-query to OpenAlex / IEEE / arXiv and",
    "also applied locally (same matching rules) as a relevance gate, so all sources share one denominator."
  ],
